                "word": "doerian",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6b299295-1b18-4ad1-a870-d8f90277f794",
                        "entry_id": "dcf5823c-5ad1-3bfd-9e59-68a0045c57d1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "doerians"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aa5bb71d-33d9-31ba-acc0-265cbec0a001",
                        "entry_id": "dcf5823c-5ad1-3bfd-9e59-68a0045c57d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Durio zibethinus een 20 tot 50 m hoge, groenblijvende boom met uitgespreide takken en een dichte kruin met zeer smakelijke maar stinkende vruchten"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e52d390-a624-417f-bccb-7c936416fad9",
                                "sense_id": "aa5bb71d-33d9-31ba-acc0-265cbec0a001",
                                "text": "Door de verkoudheid is mijn smaakzin eveneens invalide waardoor ik nu dingen kan eten die normaliter ik echt smerig vind maar die wel goed zijn voor mijn welzijn want variatie. Dus vreet ik in dit soort tijden net zolang tuinbonen en doerians tot er een maagverlamming optreedt. De dagen die me niet geheel bijblijven zijn zo tenminste nog goed voor mijn gezondheid."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a22460c0-a680-4160-8e03-9cdb4c1d3b93",
                                "sense_id": "aa5bb71d-33d9-31ba-acc0-265cbec0a001",
                                "text": "Chan Lay Choo (62) van Golden Swallow Dessert bedient een klant in het Ghim Moh Food Centre. Mijn man en ik hebben deze stal al 39 jaar. Het kachang-ijs [schaafijs -red.] is veel veranderd in de jaren. Hadden we voorheen alleen ijs met siroop, tegenwoordig bieden we allerlei toppings aan zoals mango, pinda's of doerian. Want de jongeren willen graag nieuwe smaken proberen.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "85f0db98-f831-302d-875a-af37aaef6dfb",
                        "entry_id": "dcf5823c-5ad1-3bfd-9e59-68a0045c57d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "vrucht van bovenstaande boom"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a0047002-c361-4933-a898-8fe1462ea6f1",
                        "source_entry_id": "dcf5823c-5ad1-3bfd-9e59-68a0045c57d1",
                        "source_sense_id": "aa5bb71d-33d9-31ba-acc0-265cbec0a001",
                        "source_sense_description": "een boom met zeer smakelijke maar stinkende vruchten",
                        "target_lang_word": "durian",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "durian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7a63cc4d-432b-3d9b-96a5-935b3104a7ae",
                                        "entry_id": "2a36634b-8511-3599-afed-9c47ff0523aa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several trees, genus Durio, of Southeast Asia."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "45ce3010-0e0f-3061-8a24-c1c7c5d51b6c",
                                        "entry_id": "2a36634b-8511-3599-afed-9c47ff0523aa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The spiky edible fruit of this tree, known for its strong taste and very strong, unpleasant odor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2138185-903b-4196-ae95-92fe71df35bf",
                                                "sense_id": "45ce3010-0e0f-3061-8a24-c1c7c5d51b6c",
                                                "text": "1692, Robert Boyle, General Heads for the Natural History of a Country Great or Small, London: John Taylor and S. Hedford, “Enquiries for Suratte, &c.,” p. 96,\nWhether the Betele hath such a contrariety to the Durion, that a few Leaves of that, put to a whole Shopful of Durions, will make them all rot suddenly; and whether those that have surfeited on Durions, and thereby over-heated themselves, do, by laying a Leaf or two of Betele upon their Breasts or Stomachs, immediately cure the Inflammations, and Recover."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0dde6a11-a3f0-4b40-8b14-0e2454ec1f84",
                                                "sense_id": "45ce3010-0e0f-3061-8a24-c1c7c5d51b6c",
                                                "text": "The dessert I thoroughly enjoyed, for the various fruits of Singapore are delicious. One of them, the \"durion,\" exhales a most noxious perfume, but is pleasant to the palate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "329f7a0f-b10f-459e-ab92-f91e900f270f",
                                                "sense_id": "45ce3010-0e0f-3061-8a24-c1c7c5d51b6c",
                                                "text": "Old women crouched over bags of Siamese rice, skeps of red and green peppers, purple egg-plants, bristly rambutans, pineapples, durians."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f2fc7d07-0b0b-3301-8e3a-b97f92019b9d",
                                        "entry_id": "2a36634b-8511-3599-afed-9c47ff0523aa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A deep, rich yellow colour, like that of durian flesh (also called durian yellow)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
